1
00:00:14,180 --> 00:00:18,434
( Shindo Kaneto ) This is the susuki grass .

2
00:00:19,185 --> 00:00:22,229
This place was difficult to find .

3
00:00:23,857 --> 00:00:27,860
First we went to Adachigahara ,

4
00:00:27,986 --> 00:00:30,362
where there is a legend of a she-demon ,

5
00:00:30,488 --> 00:00:33,407
but the area had been developed .

6
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:36,618
One of the assistant directors

7
00:00:37,537 --> 00:00:43,625
travelled right around Mt . Fuji looking for a place ,

8
00:00:43,752 --> 00:00:49,214
but the grass fields were either being used by the military

9
00:00:49,758 --> 00:00:51,467
or had been split up .

10
00:00:52,469 --> 00:00:56,597
He finally decided to look near the marshes ,

11
00:00:57,057 --> 00:01:02,895
and went to Inbanuma in Chiba where he found this place .

12
00:01:03,396 --> 00:01:06,815
He wanted me to take a look ,

13
00:01:08,485 --> 00:01:11,945
so I went to see .

14
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:16,116
It was just what we were looking for ,

15
00:01:16,576 --> 00:01:18,952
so we decided to film there .

16
00:01:20,413 --> 00:01:25,167
We had problems later with the stones and the bogs ,

17
00:01:25,293 --> 00:01:28,629
but I didn 't see any of that then .

18
00:01:28,755 --> 00:01:36,095
I just saw the grass rustling in the wind and thought , " This is perfect . "

19
00:01:36,554 --> 00:01:39,598
Ever since we made Ningen ,

20
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:48,315
we 'd always lodged together when filming ,

21
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:52,736
but there was no suitable place to stay nearby ,

22
00:01:52,862 --> 00:01:57,116
so we decided to build

23
00:01:58,034 --> 00:02:02,121
a prefabricated house at the site .

24
00:02:03,706 --> 00:02:06,208
The susuki grass is like having a black background .

25
00:02:07,752 --> 00:02:11,296
There is nothing to get in the way .

26
00:02:11,798 --> 00:02:14,424
It also provides a symbolic setting

27
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:18,428
for the Civil War period ,

28
00:02:18,555 --> 00:02:22,516
and I wanted the grass swaying in the wind

29
00:02:22,642 --> 00:02:25,894
to express the psychological nature of the film .

30
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:32,276
We were also working to a small budget ,

31
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:41,743
so we needed to use the minimum number of people

32
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:44,830
and this place was perfect for that .

33
00:02:45,331 --> 00:02:49,042
( Sato Kei ) I hear the production budget was 15 million yen . Is that right ?

34
00:02:50,420 --> 00:02:53,380
( Shindo ) About that .

35
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:57,009
In today 's terms , that 's about 300 million yen .

36
00:03:00,597 --> 00:03:02,556
That 's Kaji Kentaro .

37
00:03:03,725 --> 00:03:09,938
( Yoshimura Jitsuko ) They 're father and son , aren 't they ?

38
00:03:10,064 --> 00:03:13,066
( Shindo ) Yes . That 's his son-in-law .

39
00:03:17,363 --> 00:03:24,286
( Yoshimura ) The susuki grass is beautiful

40
00:03:24,954 --> 00:03:30,792
and it 's very effective ,

41
00:03:30,919 --> 00:03:35,881
psychologically .

42
00:03:38,426 --> 00:03:41,220
( Shindo ) Okamoto Taro also said

43
00:03:41,763 --> 00:03:46,225
that the grass made a fine background .

44
00:03:46,351 --> 00:03:49,561
I 'm glad that we decided to use the grass fields ,

45
00:03:50,647 --> 00:03:56,526
but it made filming very difficult .

46
00:04:00,531 --> 00:04:04,368
( Sato ) I read the production notes again the other day .

47
00:04:04,494 --> 00:04:08,163
They say how you had a flash of inspiration

48
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:16,421
about the hole which helped you to write the script .

49
00:04:18,007 --> 00:04:21,301
( Shindo ) I felt that the hole signifies

50
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:25,806
the process by which people survived .

51
00:04:28,184 --> 00:04:32,229
History tells us that

52
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:36,149
during the Civil War period

53
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:41,363
the civilian population clung on precariously

54
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:46,410
at the edge of existence ,

55
00:04:46,911 --> 00:04:50,789
which means that we are here today

56
00:04:50,915 --> 00:04:56,586
because they managed to survive .

57
00:04:56,713 --> 00:04:59,715
It shows the strength of the people

58
00:04:59,841 --> 00:05:05,304
at the bottom of the social heap .

59
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:09,641
I thought of depicting the harsh everyday life

60
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:13,103
of people who put

61
00:05:13,229 --> 00:05:18,233
food on their plates

62
00:05:18,359 --> 00:05:20,402
by murdering others .

63
00:05:21,362 --> 00:05:27,200
I don 't mean that the hole is connected directly to this in any way ,

64
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:29,494
but I wanted to use it as a metaphor

65
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:31,413
for this way of survival .

66
00:05:31,539 --> 00:05:33,457
( Sato ) The hole was like a disused well , wasn 't it ?

67
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:34,875
( Shindo ) Yes .

68
00:05:43,343 --> 00:05:46,386
How old were you when you made this , Jitsuko ?

69
00:05:46,971 --> 00:05:49,431
( Yoshimura ) I think I was about 19 .

70
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:54,353
( Shindo ) You were brimming with vitality then .

71
00:05:54,479 --> 00:05:57,230
( Yoshimura ) It was only my third film . I didn 't know anything .

72
00:05:57,357 --> 00:05:58,690
( Sato ) You look as fresh as a daisy .

73
00:05:58,816 --> 00:06:02,694
( Yoshimura ) I watched the film the other day after many years ,

74
00:06:03,321 --> 00:06:06,865
I really enjoyed it .

75
00:06:06,991 --> 00:06:12,704
The clothes we wore in the film were supposed

76
00:06:13,164 --> 00:06:16,166
to have been stolen , too .

77
00:06:16,292 --> 00:06:23,423
You gave us two sets of clothes

78
00:06:26,386 --> 00:06:31,390
and asked us to make sure they looked old ,

79
00:06:31,516 --> 00:06:33,350
so I slept in mine .

80
00:06:34,894 --> 00:06:37,479
I expect Nobuko did the same .

81
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:39,398
( Shindo ) The clothes were linen ,

82
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:41,483
I designed them myself .

83
00:06:41,943 --> 00:06:43,443
( Yoshimura ) Really ?

84
00:06:44,821 --> 00:06:46,279
( Shindo ) And I had them dyed .

85
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:50,158
Nobuko 's outfit had a crab design .

86
00:06:50,284 --> 00:06:52,077
( Yoshimura ) Mine was a fan motif .

87
00:06:59,085 --> 00:07:04,756
That was almost 40 years ago .

88
00:07:04,882 --> 00:07:07,884
I 've forgotten so much .

89
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:11,430
( Shindo ) The reason the film is still so clear

90
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:14,224
is because it was shot in black and white .

91
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:19,729
If it had been colour , the colour would have faded by now .

92
00:07:20,523 --> 00:07:25,068
( Yoshimura ) In black and white ,

93
00:07:25,653 --> 00:07:28,280
it 's more impressive .

94
00:07:29,323 --> 00:07:32,742
( Shindo ) I 'm still nostalgic about black and white now .

95
00:07:34,662 --> 00:07:38,874
When they invented film ,

96
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:43,628
they couldn 't do colour at first ,

97
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:46,965
so they started with black and white .

98
00:07:47,091 --> 00:07:51,678
But there are actually seven shades of grey in black and white .

99
00:07:53,639 --> 00:07:57,309
It represents colour in the same way

100
00:07:57,435 --> 00:08:00,770
as an Indian ink drawing .

101
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:03,523
It has that depth .

102
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:06,651
( Sato ) It is much better than badly used colour .

103
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:08,612
The susuki grass , too .

104
00:08:08,738 --> 00:08:10,155
( Yoshimura ) Absolutely .

105
00:08:10,948 --> 00:08:13,658
( Sato ) It stirs the imagination . ( Yoshimura ) That 's right .

106
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:24,211
( Shindo ) In that sense , black and white is superior .

107
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:29,883
It should have been

108
00:08:30,009 --> 00:08:35,347
invented after colour .

109
00:08:36,390 --> 00:08:41,561
All you have to do with colour is film it as it is .

110
00:08:43,064 --> 00:08:45,690
We built this set ourselves .

111
00:08:48,444 --> 00:08:50,654
( Sato ) It was tough for the assistant directors .

112
00:08:51,155 --> 00:08:52,405
( Shindo ) They had it tough .

113
00:08:53,741 --> 00:08:57,327
They were covered in cuts and bruises .

114
00:08:58,621 --> 00:09:01,373
We had eight assistant directors .

115
00:09:03,376 --> 00:09:06,920
There are usually four .

116
00:09:07,046 --> 00:09:11,383
We wanted them to gain

117
00:09:11,509 --> 00:09:14,511
a wide range of experience .

118
00:09:14,637 --> 00:09:20,642
We were an independent production company ,

119
00:09:20,768 --> 00:09:26,231
so we didn 't rely on any outside people .

120
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:29,401
We wanted to do everything ourselves .

121
00:09:29,527 --> 00:09:32,779
That 's how we did things .

122
00:09:34,782 --> 00:09:36,575
( Yoshimura ) Eight ads ?

123
00:09:37,034 --> 00:09:38,577
( Shindo ) That 's right .

124
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:41,413
( Sato ) Some were straight out of university , weren 't they ?

125
00:09:43,499 --> 00:09:47,794
( Shindo ) Some out of university , some were amateurs , some were veterans .

126
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:55,010
They were all mixed together .

127
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:57,012
It was an interesting blend .

128
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:08,523
We did everything there on location .

129
00:10:09,108 --> 00:10:11,693
It all took time and effort .

130
00:10:13,446 --> 00:10:15,947
( Sato ) If I remember right ,

131
00:10:17,158 --> 00:10:21,161
you used about 30 kilowatts of lighting .

132
00:10:21,871 --> 00:10:25,540
( Shindo ) That 's right . We used about 30 kilowatts .

133
00:10:25,666 --> 00:10:29,461
We didn 't use lights in the day .

134
00:10:31,672 --> 00:10:34,966
Just when we filmed

135
00:10:37,345 --> 00:10:40,680
in the evening or in the morning .

136
00:10:41,557 --> 00:10:46,853
( Sato ) Living on location gave you plenty of time .

137
00:10:47,355 --> 00:10:50,565
You could be very flexible .

138
00:10:51,484 --> 00:10:53,485
You could snatch a single cut

139
00:10:53,611 --> 00:10:56,196
when the wind or the light was just right .

140
00:10:56,697 --> 00:10:57,906
( Shindo ) That 's right .

141
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:02,744
It was like living and sleeping on the set .

142
00:11:04,997 --> 00:11:08,667
We could be very versatile .

143
00:11:09,210 --> 00:11:15,131
It 's an interesting way of doing things ,

144
00:11:16,634 --> 00:11:18,593
but it 's stressful because you 're shut in .

145
00:11:24,183 --> 00:11:29,354
But when you have a job to do , I think it 's best

146
00:11:29,897 --> 00:11:32,899
to keep people captive at the place they 're working .

147
00:11:34,235 --> 00:11:35,402
( Yoshimura ) Oh , really ?

148
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:40,573
( Shindo ) If you don 't do that , people can 't commit themselves .

149
00:11:41,742 --> 00:11:47,956
I think everyone wants to be kept captive ,

150
00:11:49,875 --> 00:11:54,003
so that they can get on with their work .

151
00:11:57,508 --> 00:12:03,388
( Yoshimura ) I think it 's only you who thinks that .

152
00:12:06,058 --> 00:12:08,893
We got to go to Tokyo once every three weeks .

153
00:12:09,645 --> 00:12:15,692
( Yoshimura ) Or was it every two weeks ? ( Shindo ) Every three weeks .

154
00:12:17,778 --> 00:12:21,030
( Yoshimura ) One thing I remember clearly

155
00:12:22,825 --> 00:12:25,452
is that you didn 't go back to Tokyo at all .

156
00:12:26,579 --> 00:12:28,037
Why was that ?

157
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:33,293
( Shindo ) I wanted to stay at the location continuously .

158
00:12:35,921 --> 00:12:40,133
I felt that I needed to stay there

159
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:45,096
to maintain my feel for the place .

160
00:12:46,056 --> 00:12:49,058
( Yoshimura ) Really ? I didn 't know what you were thinking .

161
00:12:49,185 --> 00:12:51,394
I just thought , " Yahoo , a holiday ! "

162
00:12:53,481 --> 00:12:56,399
I think it was two days and one night .

163
00:12:57,276 --> 00:12:59,569
I was so happy .

164
00:13:03,741 --> 00:13:05,533
I suppose there were taxis , but ...

165
00:13:05,993 --> 00:13:07,577
You wouldn 't have got taxis out there .

166
00:13:08,829 --> 00:13:13,416
We all piled into two trucks .

167
00:13:14,585 --> 00:13:18,338
It was about 10 minutes to the station , wasn 't it ?

168
00:13:18,798 --> 00:13:22,884
( Shindo ) It was four kilometres . So it was about 10 minutes .

169
00:13:25,012 --> 00:13:30,266
( Yoshimura ) We went to the station to catch the train to Tokyo .

170
00:13:30,935 --> 00:13:33,812
We were all so excited .

171
00:13:35,189 --> 00:13:40,109
We stayed one night and then came back the next evening .

172
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:45,657
We arrived at the station and the trucks were waiting for us .

173
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:49,869
Then it was back to work .

174
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:53,331
( Shindo ) This is a canal , but it looks like

175
00:13:54,083 --> 00:13:57,669
a continental river because there 's no flow .

176
00:13:57,795 --> 00:14:01,381
( Yoshimura ) It was beautiful . ( Sato ) It 's man-made .

177
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,717
It was built to take

178
00:14:04,844 --> 00:14:08,555
the overflow from the marshes down to the river .

179
00:14:10,516 --> 00:14:12,809
( Shindo ) There 's a dam a little further along .

180
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:15,603
This is where Kei appears .

181
00:14:16,730 --> 00:14:21,609
The reason I made him a monk

182
00:14:22,069 --> 00:14:26,614
was that he wouldn 't have to wear a wig .

183
00:14:27,783 --> 00:14:30,618
It would just appear that his hair had grown .

184
00:14:30,744 --> 00:14:32,495
( Yoshimura ) You were lucky , Kei .

185
00:14:32,997 --> 00:14:39,711
( Sato ) And the clothes would have kept me safe .

186
00:14:39,837 --> 00:14:41,713
( Shindo ) That 's right .

187
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:44,132
With monk 's clothes ,

188
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:48,636
he would have been safe on the road .

189
00:14:53,601 --> 00:14:56,352
( Yoshimura ) Nobuko and I both wore wigs .

190
00:14:57,021 --> 00:15:03,943
( Shindo ) But it was mostly your own hair .

191
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:09,407
We just added a little .

192
00:15:11,410 --> 00:15:17,498
It was hard work rigging the lighting here because the roof was so low . @ @ až sem pøeèteno

193
00:15:17,625 --> 00:15:20,126
( Sato ) It caught fire once . That 's right .

194
00:15:20,669 --> 00:15:25,840
You were the first one to escape when the fire started , Jitsuko .

195
00:15:25,966 --> 00:15:27,425
( Yoshimura ) Was I really ?

196
00:15:27,551 --> 00:15:30,053
( Sato ) You were the first out of the door . ( Yoshimura ) Because I was young !

197
00:15:34,892 --> 00:15:37,977
( Shindo ) It was hard going for everyone .

198
00:15:38,103 --> 00:15:46,653
But because you were all held captive in one place ,

199
00:15:48,489 --> 00:15:52,784
there was nowhere to escape to and we had plenty of time .

200
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:55,036
( Yoshimura ) Yes , we had lots of time .

201
00:16:00,209 --> 00:16:02,251
( Shindo ) Because we had so much time ,

202
00:16:02,378 --> 00:16:06,214
it felt as if we could be relaxed about things . Mind you , it was hot .

203
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:08,383
( Sato ) God , it was hot !

204
00:16:09,885 --> 00:16:11,719
( Shindo ) Not only that ...

205
00:16:12,805 --> 00:16:18,184
The reeds and the scenery may look cool ,

206
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:22,355
but the hot , stifling smell of the grass was terrible .

207
00:16:23,107 --> 00:16:26,317
I remember Kei saying that

208
00:16:26,443 --> 00:16:31,072
we ran the risk of catching a nasty disease from the mites

209
00:16:31,198 --> 00:16:33,241
if we filmed there .

210
00:16:35,369 --> 00:16:39,664
We were lucky though ,

211
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:42,000
because no one got sick .

212
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:46,546
( Sato ) When Masaki Kobayashi was filming The Human Condition ,

213
00:16:47,548 --> 00:16:52,552
up in Sarobetsu in Hokkaido ,

214
00:16:53,178 --> 00:16:59,851
the locals warned him about the danger of disease from mites .

215
00:16:59,977 --> 00:17:03,062
When they had to go into the swamp ,

216
00:17:03,188 --> 00:17:07,650
they wrapped themselves in plastic underneath their clothes .

217
00:17:08,944 --> 00:17:11,738
They were worried , but they didn 't catch anything .

218
00:17:12,197 --> 00:17:17,285
( Shindo ) It would have been quite natural to get sick in a place like that .

219
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:18,995
( Sato ) That 's right .

220
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:21,456
I didn 't know about it until later ,

221
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:24,959
but the area where the marsh meets the reed beds

222
00:17:25,085 --> 00:17:27,670
is a very primitive environment .

223
00:17:28,672 --> 00:17:31,924
It was like that tens of thousands of years ago .

224
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:36,512
It looks as if you could walk along quite easily ,

225
00:17:37,056 --> 00:17:40,349
but it 's so boggy you would sink in up to your waist .

226
00:17:43,771 --> 00:17:48,066
( Sato ) Does it belong to the Water Agency ?

227
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:51,944
( Shindo ) Yes , it 's managed by the Water Agency .

228
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:55,156
We got permission to use it ,

229
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:58,993
and we built the set there .

230
00:17:59,119 --> 00:18:03,831
Because we did it here , we didn 't have to worry about onlookers .

231
00:18:03,957 --> 00:18:09,087
We basically had a cast of three .

232
00:18:10,255 --> 00:18:14,383
It was good because we could focus that way .

233
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:26,562
You wouldn 't have been able to appear in anything else ,

234
00:18:27,481 --> 00:18:30,399
with a beard like that anyway .

235
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:38,491
It was lucky for us .

236
00:18:38,617 --> 00:18:41,661
Mind you , it was rough for the actors , wasn 't it ?

237
00:18:41,787 --> 00:18:44,413
( Sato ) I wasn 't much in demand anyway .

238
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:47,750
( Shindo ) That 's not true .

239
00:18:49,336 --> 00:18:53,297
( Sato ) I arrived at the set about one week

240
00:18:53,423 --> 00:18:57,677
after shooting had started .

241
00:18:58,929 --> 00:19:02,682
There was a bath and a toilet by then .

242
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:06,769
( Yoshimura ) There were separate toilets for men and women .

243
00:19:06,895 --> 00:19:10,857
( Sato ) I remember these small , yellow

244
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:14,986
poisonous moths appeared once .

245
00:19:16,196 --> 00:19:21,450
One of the crew was sitting in the bath

246
00:19:21,577 --> 00:19:24,537
with a rash all over his body .

247
00:19:27,374 --> 00:19:31,711
( Shindo ) Talk about moths to the flame .

248
00:19:31,837 --> 00:19:33,963
The insects would emerge in swarms in the evening .

249
00:19:34,089 --> 00:19:36,132
( Sato ) It was amazing .

250
00:19:36,925 --> 00:19:40,052
( Shindo ) I thought there were only

251
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:45,099
one or two types of insect that come out at night ,

252
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:47,852
but there were scores of different types .

253
00:19:47,978 --> 00:19:49,770
( Yoshimura ) Were there that many ?

254
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:53,107
( Shindo ) One type would arrive en masse ,

255
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:56,736
stay for a week and then disappear .

256
00:19:58,906 --> 00:20:01,115
Then a different type would turn up .

257
00:20:01,909 --> 00:20:06,954
The insects were terrible . They would drop to the floor ,

258
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:10,166
and the crawfish would come to eat them .

259
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:17,924
( Sato ) We used a light trap and caught hundreds of them .

260
00:20:18,383 --> 00:20:21,802
( Shindo ) They came pouring in and dropped down dead .

261
00:20:21,929 --> 00:20:26,474
( Sato ) We burnt them all with gasoline . It was crazy .

262
00:20:29,645 --> 00:20:32,230
When we filmed at night , the insects would come

263
00:20:32,689 --> 00:20:36,442
flying into your mouth when you tried to say your lines .

264
00:20:41,323 --> 00:20:43,950
( Shindo ) That 's right .

265
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:49,664
But the daytime was a hard grind , too .

266
00:20:49,790 --> 00:20:53,709
( Sato ) The ADs had it tough .

267
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:56,963
( Shindo ) There wasn 't much to do at night ,

268
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:59,423
so we passed the time cremating insects .

269
00:21:05,264 --> 00:21:10,142
( Sato ) You would go to bed early because you don 't drink .

270
00:21:10,936 --> 00:21:15,815
But a few of us would sit out on the embankment ,

271
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:18,526
drinking till midnight .

272
00:21:18,652 --> 00:21:22,280
( Yoshimura ) You drank on the embankment ? I didn 't know that .

273
00:21:22,406 --> 00:21:25,658
( Sato ) If we had sat outside , it would have been too noisy .

274
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:28,703
( Shindo ) It 's slightly cooler out there by the river , too .

275
00:21:29,454 --> 00:21:32,081
Sitting and drinking on the riverbank .

276
00:21:32,207 --> 00:21:39,255
It 's not something you get to do every day .

277
00:21:42,342 --> 00:21:44,385
( Yoshimura ) It was a priceless experience .

278
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:49,640
( Shindo ) If we 'd had the money ,

279
00:21:50,642 --> 00:21:53,894
we could have provided all sorts of facilities ,

280
00:21:54,021 --> 00:21:57,732
but I think it was better this way .

281
00:21:58,859 --> 00:22:05,114
This sort of primitive style is better , isn 't it ?

282
00:22:05,866 --> 00:22:07,408
( Sato ) I think so .

283
00:22:07,534 --> 00:22:11,829
( Shindo ) Our primitive lifestyle matched the film itself .

284
00:22:11,955 --> 00:22:15,875
Simple food and cheap dried fish .

285
00:22:19,254 --> 00:22:25,134
You 'd think we 'd have all kinds of fresh fish ,

286
00:22:25,260 --> 00:22:30,097
staying next to a swamp .

287
00:22:30,223 --> 00:22:33,893
But we didn 't .

288
00:22:36,855 --> 00:22:39,815
( Sato ) There were grass carp .

289
00:22:41,026 --> 00:22:44,904
( Yoshimura ) Were they big ? ( Sato ) About one metre long .

290
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:47,281
( Shindo ) Grass carp were introduced from China .

291
00:22:47,407 --> 00:22:48,908
There were snakehead mullet , too .

292
00:22:49,701 --> 00:22:54,330
They can actually come onto the land for a while .

293
00:22:55,457 --> 00:22:56,874
They look a bit like snakes .

294
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:00,586
( Sato ) The grass carp ate up all the small fish in the area .

295
00:23:00,712 --> 00:23:03,422
They built a fish pen for them on the bank ,

296
00:23:03,548 --> 00:23:06,300
but they were still wiped out .

297
00:23:07,636 --> 00:23:12,765
( Shindo ) They caught the small fish and put them in a fish pen .

298
00:23:15,644 --> 00:23:20,731
Didn 't you have moxibustion treatment on your stomach

299
00:23:20,857 --> 00:23:25,403
to increase your weight when we were doing Ningen , Kei ?

300
00:23:25,529 --> 00:23:28,739
You have plenty of meat on you here .

301
00:23:29,324 --> 00:23:34,620
( Sato ) Ningen was two years before this .

302
00:23:34,746 --> 00:23:40,835
I only weighed 48 kg at the time .

303
00:23:42,421 --> 00:23:47,466
After six months of treatment , I was up to 73 kg .

304
00:23:48,969 --> 00:23:51,220
Onibaba was only two years after that .

305
00:23:51,346 --> 00:23:55,141
( Shindo ) You were a bit chubby then . ( Sato ) I 'd lost a bit of weight then .

306
00:23:55,892 --> 00:23:59,770
I was about 70 kg here .

307
00:24:00,897 --> 00:24:06,152
( Shindo ) Yes , I thought you were quite big then .

308
00:24:06,278 --> 00:24:08,863
( Yoshimura ) Is that a snakehead mullet you 're holding ?

309
00:24:08,989 --> 00:24:13,993
( Shindo ) No , it 's a crucian carp . ( Sato ) A big one .

310
00:24:18,582 --> 00:24:21,792
There wouldn 't have been any grass carp or snakehead mullet

311
00:24:21,918 --> 00:24:24,170
in those days .

312
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:27,465
They were only introduced after the war .

313
00:24:33,597 --> 00:24:37,600
( Shindo ) 19 years old ? You 're just brimming with youth .

314
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:40,519
( Sato ) Your skin is glowing .

315
00:24:42,814 --> 00:24:48,652
( Yoshimura ) I watched the film again a few days ago ,

316
00:24:48,778 --> 00:24:53,199
I could hardly believe I was so young once . It made me happy to see .

317
00:24:53,325 --> 00:24:57,244
( Shindo ) Of course . That 's natural .

318
00:25:00,916 --> 00:25:06,212
The mud beneath the reeds was like a quagmire .

319
00:25:06,671 --> 00:25:10,341
It was very unpleasant , but we were lucky

320
00:25:10,467 --> 00:25:12,760
that no one got sick .

321
00:25:14,513 --> 00:25:17,014
( Yoshimura ) We were very lucky .

322
00:25:17,140 --> 00:25:19,892
( Sato ) We didn 't take any precautions either .

323
00:25:20,018 --> 00:25:23,938
( Shindo ) We didn 't have any medical facilities .

324
00:25:24,064 --> 00:25:25,773
( Shindo ) Our budget didn 't stretch to that .

325
00:25:25,899 --> 00:25:28,150
( Yoshimura ) We didn 't have any inoculations .

326
00:25:28,276 --> 00:25:30,903
( Sato ) We didn 't do anything like that .

327
00:25:31,655 --> 00:25:38,661
( Shindo ) None of the ADs got sick either .

328
00:25:38,787 --> 00:25:40,371
( Yoshimura ) That 's right .

329
00:25:40,997 --> 00:25:47,211
( Shindo ) When the ADs got stressed out ,

330
00:25:47,337 --> 00:25:50,673
they 'd run marathons to the railway station in the evening .

331
00:25:51,258 --> 00:25:53,717
( Sato ) Did they do that ?

332
00:25:53,843 --> 00:26:00,099
( Shindo ) They wanted to burn up their energy .

333
00:26:03,645 --> 00:26:05,729
( Yoshimura ) I didn 't know that .

334
00:26:05,855 --> 00:26:09,858
( Shindo ) The day after a holiday ,

335
00:26:10,318 --> 00:26:13,988
I would sometimes go up and wait on the embankment

336
00:26:14,114 --> 00:26:21,662
and would watch as people came trickling back in ones and twos .

337
00:26:21,788 --> 00:26:25,291
I was relieved to see them .

338
00:26:25,417 --> 00:26:30,838
They returned but they 'd been thinking .

339
00:26:32,549 --> 00:26:34,800
( Sato ) Did you think they 'd escape ?

340
00:26:34,926 --> 00:26:39,930
( Shindo ) Yes . I thought some people would run away .

341
00:26:40,056 --> 00:26:44,310
( Yoshimura ) But no one did ? ( Shindo ) No one did .

342
00:26:46,605 --> 00:26:53,611
Maybe they just didn 't have the time to think of escaping .

343
00:26:55,822 --> 00:27:01,535
( Sato ) That was the year of the Tokyo Olympics .

344
00:27:02,454 --> 00:27:06,040
Even when you got away to Tokyo , it was noisy and crowded .

345
00:27:08,126 --> 00:27:13,631
( Shindo ) You don 't get many opportunities

346
00:27:13,757 --> 00:27:16,050
for a group of people to focus

347
00:27:16,176 --> 00:27:22,181
on a single task like this .

348
00:27:25,518 --> 00:27:30,439
( Sato ) The samurai over there is Tanaka Hiroshi .

349
00:27:32,192 --> 00:27:35,277
He became famous doing that ham commercial .

350
00:27:35,403 --> 00:27:38,864
He was a stand-in for Mifune , wasn 't he ?

351
00:27:39,908 --> 00:27:42,368
It was the boneless ham .

352
00:27:43,578 --> 00:27:49,375
( Shindo ) He 's actually quite small , but he 's wearing armour .

353
00:27:51,086 --> 00:27:54,338
It 's not funny ,

354
00:27:55,173 --> 00:27:57,299
but he almost drowned .

355
00:27:58,718 --> 00:28:04,181
I could have filmed the scene in separate cuts ,

356
00:28:04,307 --> 00:28:07,476
but I wanted to film the whole scene to give it power .

357
00:28:08,186 --> 00:28:11,939
That 's why we did it this way .

358
00:28:14,192 --> 00:28:18,946
That 's how we did it , but it was serious .

359
00:28:19,072 --> 00:28:21,073
( Sato ) I was really worried .

360
00:28:21,199 --> 00:28:24,702
( Shindo ) You were impatient . ( Sato ) No , I was worried !

361
00:28:25,453 --> 00:28:27,663
( Shindo ) In the film , I mean .

362
00:28:28,373 --> 00:28:31,667
You were impatient , waiting for him to arrive .

363
00:28:32,377 --> 00:28:34,420
You spear him here .

364
00:28:37,257 --> 00:28:39,550
( Yoshimura ) After all that effort to swim across ...

365
00:28:49,811 --> 00:28:51,812
( Sato ) The water was dirty .

366
00:28:51,938 --> 00:28:56,191
( Shindo ) It looks clean , but it was dirty .

367
00:29:01,781 --> 00:29:03,407
( Sato ) That 's Yamaguchi .

368
00:29:11,374 --> 00:29:15,753
Tanaka was Terajima Mitsugu 's son , wasn 't he ?

369
00:29:15,879 --> 00:29:21,925
( Shindo ) I think he was related to the wife of the cameraman .

370
00:29:23,970 --> 00:29:28,348
That 's how he came to be with us .

371
00:29:28,475 --> 00:29:32,269
I used him because he also did some stunt work .

372
00:29:33,271 --> 00:29:35,564
There was no point in rehearsing this .

373
00:29:35,690 --> 00:29:40,944
They just had to react as they went along .

374
00:29:47,827 --> 00:29:50,662
They turned this into a ballet in America .

375
00:30:04,302 --> 00:30:10,057
An American production company

376
00:30:10,183 --> 00:30:15,270
is interested in buying the story .

377
00:30:15,897 --> 00:30:18,732
It 's a simple story .

378
00:30:20,610 --> 00:30:24,530
It 's a very traditional folk tale ,

379
00:30:27,700 --> 00:30:30,869
and this folk tale has

380
00:30:30,995 --> 00:30:36,875
the man and woman relationship .

381
00:30:37,001 --> 00:30:41,088
It 's simple .

382
00:30:44,676 --> 00:30:50,055
( Sato ) It was about this time that Tonoyama stopped drinking .

383
00:30:50,181 --> 00:30:56,228
( Shindo ) That 's right . He shouted out , " I 'm giving up drinking from today ! "

384
00:30:57,480 --> 00:31:02,109
( Sato ) But nobody paid a blind bit of notice .

385
00:31:05,029 --> 00:31:10,659
( Shindo ) Why did you used to call Tonoyama-san

386
00:31:10,785 --> 00:31:14,788
by the nickname oyabin ?

387
00:31:14,914 --> 00:31:19,459
( Sato ) It comes from the words oyabun meaning " boss "

388
00:31:19,586 --> 00:31:23,338
and hagechabin meaning " baldy " .

389
00:31:33,850 --> 00:31:39,146
( Yoshimura ) I worked with Tonoyama

390
00:31:39,272 --> 00:31:42,941
on films after this .

391
00:31:43,443 --> 00:31:46,236
He was very shy .

392
00:31:48,197 --> 00:31:52,701
I remember if I teased him ,

393
00:31:52,827 --> 00:31:59,416
he would just look down and grin sheepishly .

394
00:32:01,210 --> 00:32:06,798
( Shindo ) He was a cultured man .

395
00:32:07,258 --> 00:32:08,967
( Sato ) He was intelligent .

396
00:32:09,093 --> 00:32:13,388
( Shindo ) Yes , and he was a humble man .

397
00:32:14,140 --> 00:32:20,479
He was a cultured man and intelligent ,

398
00:32:22,065 --> 00:32:24,691
and a funny person .

399
00:32:25,234 --> 00:32:31,281
He was an interesting fellow .

400
00:32:44,045 --> 00:32:48,966
( Yoshimura ) I think everybody had times

401
00:32:49,926 --> 00:32:56,473
when they were stressed out

402
00:32:56,599 --> 00:33:01,353
and wanted to go home .

403
00:33:04,148 --> 00:33:11,363
I had that feeling at times ,

404
00:33:11,864 --> 00:33:14,908
but Nobuko looked after me .

405
00:33:15,034 --> 00:33:18,787
I can only remember the happy times now .

406
00:33:20,331 --> 00:33:26,461
( Shindo ) You were young ,

407
00:33:27,005 --> 00:33:33,552
and everyone was eager .

408
00:33:33,678 --> 00:33:40,017
I just let people do their thing .

409
00:33:44,439 --> 00:33:48,525
You were all enthusiastic .

410
00:33:48,651 --> 00:33:52,654
( Yoshimura ) Did we rehearse ?

411
00:33:52,780 --> 00:33:58,076
( Shindo ) No . ( Sato ) We just did a camera test .

412
00:33:59,412 --> 00:34:04,833
( Yoshimura ) The set was only about five minutes from where we stayed .

413
00:34:04,959 --> 00:34:08,503
I thought we did a bit of rehearsal ,

414
00:34:09,797 --> 00:34:15,260
but it 's over thirty years ago and I can 't remember .

415
00:34:15,386 --> 00:34:17,971
( Sato ) Maybe you did some practice by yourself .

416
00:34:18,097 --> 00:34:21,308
( Yoshimura ) I wasn 't that serious .

417
00:34:21,434 --> 00:34:25,520
( Shindo ) There was no point in rehearsal .

418
00:34:26,230 --> 00:34:32,778
There 's no way to rehearse how to bite into a chunk of meat .

419
00:34:33,821 --> 00:34:40,952
It wasn 't a specific type of acting .

420
00:34:42,538 --> 00:34:48,376
We were portraying humans reduced

421
00:34:48,503 --> 00:34:51,755
almost to the level of beasts .

422
00:34:51,881 --> 00:34:55,801
There 's no way to rehearse that .

423
00:34:55,927 --> 00:35:00,555
Simply staying in that place together

424
00:35:02,642 --> 00:35:05,936
was a sufficient rehearsal .

425
00:35:06,062 --> 00:35:10,148
( Yoshimura ) That feeling that we were all in it together

426
00:35:10,650 --> 00:35:16,822
was very different from the two films I 'd done before that .

427
00:35:17,824 --> 00:35:26,873
( Shindo ) I went to Montreal last year , 1999 ,

428
00:35:28,668 --> 00:35:36,550
and screened Onibaba and The Naked Island .

429
00:35:36,676 --> 00:35:44,391
The people I met in the cafés knew Onibaba .

430
00:35:44,517 --> 00:35:52,107
When we met , they would all say , " Ah , Onibaba , Onibaba ! "

431
00:35:52,233 --> 00:35:58,905
You could hear them , " Onibaba , Onibaba . "

432
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:06,663
It 's very simple and straightforward ,

433
00:36:06,789 --> 00:36:09,666
and people overseas appreciated it as well .

434
00:36:10,126 --> 00:36:14,171
( Sato ) It was very popular .

435
00:36:17,341 --> 00:36:23,138
( Shindo ) " Onibaba , Onibaba , " they said !

436
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:34,191
I took four prints and they screened them two at a time

437
00:36:34,942 --> 00:36:36,985
at the main venue .

438
00:36:44,535 --> 00:36:51,416
Film made its appearance in the 20th century ,

439
00:36:51,542 --> 00:36:54,628
and now you can see Nobuko like this ,

440
00:36:54,754 --> 00:36:59,758
even though she 's no longer with us .

441
00:37:00,218 --> 00:37:06,848
In some respect , the viewpoint of life and death has changed .

442
00:37:07,391 --> 00:37:10,977
The voice remains .

443
00:37:13,564 --> 00:37:20,028
( Yoshimura ) When I saw the titles at the beginning ,

444
00:37:20,154 --> 00:37:25,659
I was shocked to think that so many of those people

445
00:37:26,327 --> 00:37:30,247
have passed away .

446
00:37:30,373 --> 00:37:33,250
We might be the only three left .

447
00:37:33,376 --> 00:37:37,170
( Shindo ) Kuroda , the cameraman ,

448
00:37:37,296 --> 00:37:41,424
the lighting man ,

449
00:37:42,718 --> 00:37:49,099
Shige who did the make-up .

450
00:37:53,938 --> 00:38:00,110
( Yoshimura ) Uno , Tonoyama , Tanaka

451
00:38:00,236 --> 00:38:04,155
and Sonesho are all dead .

452
00:38:04,282 --> 00:38:09,869
It 's just the three of us .

453
00:38:09,996 --> 00:38:15,792
And you 're the fittest of us all .

454
00:38:15,918 --> 00:38:21,131
( Shindo ) I think not . I 'm 89 years old .

455
00:38:22,925 --> 00:38:27,220
( Sato ) How old were you when you made Onibaba ?

456
00:38:27,346 --> 00:38:31,683
( Shindo ) Fifty-five .

457
00:38:32,768 --> 00:38:35,562
I was fit then .

458
00:38:43,321 --> 00:38:46,948
Breath is important

459
00:38:49,327 --> 00:38:53,663
for acting and for directing .

460
00:38:53,789 --> 00:38:57,917
If you have no breath

461
00:38:58,044 --> 00:39:05,050
left in your lungs after you have breathed out ,

462
00:39:05,718 --> 00:39:11,765
you lose your power .

463
00:39:14,310 --> 00:39:19,356
When your breath is used up and doesn 't come out anymore ,

464
00:39:19,482 --> 00:39:22,817
it is useless .

465
00:39:33,371 --> 00:39:36,164
( Yoshimura ) You 've gone crazy here , Kei .

466
00:39:45,216 --> 00:39:49,677
( Shindo ) The film doesn 't look at all dated .

467
00:39:49,804 --> 00:39:52,889
( Yoshimura ) That 's right .

468
00:40:15,704 --> 00:40:23,211
( Shindo ) I added the cooing of pigeons

469
00:40:23,671 --> 00:40:25,672
to the scene when you are running .

470
00:40:28,175 --> 00:40:32,762
I heard that pigeons are known for their fecundity ,

471
00:40:32,888 --> 00:40:38,685
so I added the sound to the scene where Jitsuko

472
00:40:38,811 --> 00:40:43,773
is running through the grass in the grip of desire .

473
00:40:43,899 --> 00:40:46,985
I added it for effect .

474
00:40:47,111 --> 00:40:49,988
( Yoshimura ) I didn 't know that .

475
00:40:55,995 --> 00:41:01,374
( Shindo ) Hayashi Hikaru also came to the set .

476
00:41:04,503 --> 00:41:07,422
( Yoshimura ) I ran like the wind then .

477
00:41:07,548 --> 00:41:10,008
I was covered in scratches .

478
00:41:11,802 --> 00:41:16,764
If I tried that now ,

479
00:41:19,226 --> 00:41:23,980
I 'd have a heart attack .

480
00:41:31,238 --> 00:41:36,367
( Shindo ) We could make it appear

481
00:41:36,494 --> 00:41:40,538
to be night ,

482
00:41:41,332 --> 00:41:46,211
because we filmed in black and white .

483
00:41:46,337 --> 00:41:49,088
If you adjust the contrast ,

484
00:41:49,215 --> 00:41:52,675
use a red filter

485
00:41:52,801 --> 00:41:58,681
and emphasise the black ,

486
00:41:58,807 --> 00:42:05,230
then you are able to turn day into night .

487
00:42:05,356 --> 00:42:09,817
This technique was developed for black and white film .

488
00:42:09,944 --> 00:42:12,904
I 'm not sure who invented it .

489
00:42:13,030 --> 00:42:16,574
( Sato ) Can 't you do it with colour ? ( Shindo ) No , not with colour .

490
00:42:16,700 --> 00:42:18,451
The picture would be dark .

491
00:42:18,577 --> 00:42:21,579
It just becomes darker .

492
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:25,124
There 's an effect that occurs ...

493
00:42:25,251 --> 00:42:32,840
If you increase the contrast in black and white film ,

494
00:42:34,677 --> 00:42:39,639
it has the effect of accentuating the white ,

495
00:42:39,765 --> 00:42:41,224
so the image becomes clearer .

496
00:42:49,817 --> 00:42:53,319
The effect can be quite strange .

497
00:42:54,071 --> 00:42:55,947
It 's very effective .

498
00:42:58,409 --> 00:43:02,870
We filmed the susuki grass

499
00:43:02,997 --> 00:43:09,043
with and without lights .

500
00:43:11,005 --> 00:43:15,466
If the lights are switched on ,

501
00:43:16,594 --> 00:43:20,972
the sky becomes dark

502
00:43:21,098 --> 00:43:28,563
and the grass appears white .

503
00:43:30,149 --> 00:43:37,322
Without light , the grass becomes black and the sky white .

504
00:43:37,448 --> 00:43:41,409
The two can be used as a montage to create an interesting effect .

505
00:43:43,412 --> 00:43:47,665
I took this shot at about 3.5 times speed .

506
00:43:50,044 --> 00:43:54,172
They usually shoot running giraffes

507
00:43:57,926 --> 00:44:03,139
and other animals at between

508
00:44:03,265 --> 00:44:09,145
3.5 and 5 times normal speed .

509
00:44:21,992 --> 00:44:25,828
From the start , I wanted the swaying of the susuki grass

510
00:44:25,954 --> 00:44:32,585
to express the psychological nature of the film .

511
00:44:46,183 --> 00:44:49,727
( Yoshimura ) Neither Nobuko nor I had names ,

512
00:44:50,604 --> 00:44:57,860
but Hachi and my dead husband did .

513
00:44:57,986 --> 00:45:00,113
( Shindo ) I used you as symbols .

514
00:45:00,239 --> 00:45:02,407
( Yoshimura ) Why was that ?

515
00:45:02,533 --> 00:45:08,830
( Shindo ) ... to represent people .

516
00:45:13,252 --> 00:45:19,090
As a person who would be able

517
00:45:19,216 --> 00:45:21,926
to represent the populace .

518
00:45:43,991 --> 00:45:49,912
You can only get this kind of effect with black and white film .

519
00:45:57,880 --> 00:46:00,923
We couldn 't film on cloudy days .

520
00:46:05,012 --> 00:46:09,182
You don 't get the effect of black and white film

521
00:46:09,308 --> 00:46:10,975
unless you have clear blue skies .

522
00:46:11,101 --> 00:46:14,687
In the old days , we would wait for clear weather to film .

523
00:46:14,813 --> 00:46:20,318
Nowadays you can get vivid colours regardless

524
00:46:20,861 --> 00:46:24,197
of whether it 's cloudy or not .

525
00:46:24,323 --> 00:46:27,366
There 's no need to fear the clouds ,

526
00:46:28,035 --> 00:46:30,870
you can shoot to your heart 's content .

527
00:46:31,538 --> 00:46:35,458
On the other side of the coin ,

528
00:46:36,460 --> 00:46:42,340
people now take less care in composing their shots .

529
00:47:06,323 --> 00:47:11,327
How long did you stay on location ?

530
00:47:14,748 --> 00:47:20,253
( Sato ) Was it June we started ?

531
00:47:24,591 --> 00:47:28,302
( Yoshimura ) I think I was there for three months .

532
00:47:35,143 --> 00:47:37,979
( Shindo ) It took a long time ,

533
00:47:40,065 --> 00:47:43,943
because we had to wait for the weather .

534
00:47:44,444 --> 00:47:47,989
( Sato ) According to these records ,

535
00:47:48,907 --> 00:47:53,744
filming started 30th June 1964 and I joined in July .

536
00:47:55,163 --> 00:47:58,457
We finished up on 9th September .

537
00:48:17,436 --> 00:48:20,605
Shindo , Kuroda and Shirota

538
00:48:21,648 --> 00:48:25,067
left on the two o 'clock train

539
00:48:25,944 --> 00:48:31,198
on 9 October .

540
00:48:32,034 --> 00:48:36,829
It says that they departed under leaden skies with heavy hearts .

541
00:48:39,833 --> 00:48:46,255
( Shindo ) Whenever I start a new project ,

542
00:48:46,381 --> 00:48:51,093
it feels as if I 'm beginning a new life .

543
00:48:52,763 --> 00:48:55,890
And when the time comes

544
00:48:56,350 --> 00:49:00,061
when the work ends ,

545
00:49:00,687 --> 00:49:04,065
it feels as if one life

546
00:49:04,191 --> 00:49:08,194
has come to an end .

547
00:49:10,864 --> 00:49:17,036
( Sato ) When an actor has played his part , he goes home .

548
00:49:17,829 --> 00:49:22,792
When the soundman and other crew have done their jobs , they go home .

549
00:49:24,002 --> 00:49:26,629
The director stays till the end .

550
00:49:34,972 --> 00:49:37,306
( Shindo ) That 's right .

551
00:49:37,432 --> 00:49:40,351
I suppose it 's mentally

552
00:49:41,561 --> 00:49:46,148
and physically tiring .

553
00:49:48,318 --> 00:49:52,571
But it 's the actors

554
00:49:52,698 --> 00:49:56,075
who do the running

555
00:49:57,411 --> 00:50:01,539
and all the director has to do

556
00:50:04,751 --> 00:50:08,212
is watch them perform .

557
00:50:08,338 --> 00:50:12,174
I admire actors .

558
00:50:13,552 --> 00:50:15,094
( Yoshimura ) Thank you !

559
00:50:18,557 --> 00:50:22,685
( Shindo ) Mind you , I suppose they do it

560
00:50:23,228 --> 00:50:25,229
because it 's interesting ,

561
00:50:27,941 --> 00:50:31,819
so I shouldn 't worry too much about them .

562
00:50:33,530 --> 00:50:37,867
But actors are a breed apart .

563
00:50:40,203 --> 00:50:43,748
( Sato ) I always have a bit

564
00:50:43,874 --> 00:50:48,919
of a guilty conscience as an actor .

565
00:50:49,880 --> 00:50:51,714
Whether it 's film or stage ,

566
00:50:56,094 --> 00:51:00,973
the actor works to a script

567
00:51:04,394 --> 00:51:09,356
and has someone to direct him ,

568
00:51:10,025 --> 00:51:13,611
and yet he plays it as if it is all his own work .

569
00:51:14,404 --> 00:51:18,324
It 's like he 's cheating the audience and the director .

570
00:51:19,993 --> 00:51:23,037
( Yoshimura ) Because I 'm impudent , I don 't feel like that .

571
00:51:23,163 --> 00:51:25,081
( Sato ) It 's shyness .

572
00:51:27,250 --> 00:51:30,127
( Shindo ) I can understand that .

573
00:51:30,837 --> 00:51:36,342
A director also has a feeling of impotence .

574
00:51:37,677 --> 00:51:39,929
Because he doesn 't actually do it .

575
00:51:41,473 --> 00:51:47,603
He orders people about , but doesn 't actually do it himself .

576
00:51:49,106 --> 00:51:54,693
He leaves everything to other people .

577
00:51:55,320 --> 00:51:59,115
It 's like there 's a glass wall

578
00:51:59,241 --> 00:52:03,536
in front of you .

579
00:52:04,955 --> 00:52:08,874
It 's frustrating .

580
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:11,585
( Sato ) Yes , it must be frustrating for a director .

581
00:52:12,879 --> 00:52:15,798
Especially when the actors can 't get it right !

582
00:52:19,928 --> 00:52:22,054
( Shindo ) No , it 's not that .

583
00:52:22,931 --> 00:52:29,103
If the film turns out well , the director gets the credit ,

584
00:52:29,229 --> 00:52:37,069
but he didn 't really do it himself .

585
00:52:40,907 --> 00:52:43,951
It 's funny , when I speak to actors

586
00:52:45,036 --> 00:52:49,707
who do stage work ,

587
00:52:50,876 --> 00:52:55,004
they still find it interesting

588
00:52:55,630 --> 00:53:03,220
even when they are performing the same role ,

589
00:53:05,515 --> 00:53:07,099
day after day .

590
00:53:08,643 --> 00:53:10,394
( Sato ) Not me .

591
00:53:13,565 --> 00:53:15,608
I like a one-off performance .

592
00:53:16,401 --> 00:53:19,320
I don 't mind rehearsing for two weeks

593
00:53:19,446 --> 00:53:21,197
or a month .

594
00:53:21,323 --> 00:53:28,621
That 's necessary to understand the script .

595
00:53:28,747 --> 00:53:33,250
But I just want to do one performance .

596
00:53:33,919 --> 00:53:37,254
( Shindo ) It 's a different audience every day .

597
00:53:37,380 --> 00:53:40,216
( Sato ) That 's true .

598
00:53:41,593 --> 00:53:46,430
But I like to do it just once .

599
00:53:46,556 --> 00:53:49,016
( Shindo ) I 'm the same .

600
00:53:56,441 --> 00:54:00,778
As a director , I only want to shoot a scene once .

601
00:54:03,573 --> 00:54:06,450
I don 't want to go back and do it again .

602
00:54:07,494 --> 00:54:10,162
It doesn 't work well if I do .

603
00:54:10,622 --> 00:54:14,500
Even if you see something that 's not right

604
00:54:14,626 --> 00:54:20,089
in the rushes and you decide to retake it ,

605
00:54:21,633 --> 00:54:25,427
it 's not good enough .

606
00:54:27,472 --> 00:54:33,394
If you retake it , it never looks right .

607
00:54:35,563 --> 00:54:40,609
It 's as if you have painted over the top of it .

608
00:54:41,236 --> 00:54:43,612
You need to start with a blank sheet .

609
00:54:45,156 --> 00:54:47,992
It 's all or nothing .

610
00:54:48,118 --> 00:54:51,745
( Sato ) First time is best for acting as well .

611
00:54:53,415 --> 00:54:55,416
( Yoshimura ) There is a tension in it .

612
00:54:55,542 --> 00:54:58,210
( Sato ) From the second try onward ,

613
00:54:58,336 --> 00:55:02,965
you are aiming for safety .

614
00:55:06,011 --> 00:55:09,638
( Shindo ) Actors are artists .

615
00:55:11,516 --> 00:55:13,392
They are creative .

616
00:55:14,269 --> 00:55:20,983
They create something from unknown spaces within ,

617
00:55:21,484 --> 00:55:25,696
using their bodies

618
00:55:27,949 --> 00:55:31,493
and their actions .

619
00:55:33,830 --> 00:55:39,793
They work from morning to night ,

620
00:55:40,920 --> 00:55:44,757
but that doesn 't mean they do it best

621
00:55:45,216 --> 00:55:48,719
at the end of the day .

622
00:55:51,931 --> 00:55:56,518
Mizoguchi Kenji said the same thing .

623
00:55:58,396 --> 00:56:03,025
He would sometimes do test runs for a whole day ,

624
00:56:03,151 --> 00:56:08,238
and he said that people often got worse the more they tried .

625
00:56:08,365 --> 00:56:11,784
( Yoshimura ) Maybe because they were tired !

626
00:56:14,537 --> 00:56:17,915
( Shindo ) We burned tyres to get the smoke here .

627
00:56:18,041 --> 00:56:22,795
It was really hard work just getting over there to do it .

628
00:56:24,089 --> 00:56:28,217
Not for me , but for the ADs !

629
00:56:28,343 --> 00:56:30,386
We just watched it .

630
00:56:33,306 --> 00:56:39,436
It was the little things like that which took time .

631
00:56:40,438 --> 00:56:42,481
That 's why we were there three months .

632
00:56:45,402 --> 00:56:48,821
For example , if a clump of reeds fell down ,

633
00:56:48,947 --> 00:56:52,116
we would have to bring some more in and prop them up .

634
00:56:54,077 --> 00:56:58,288
They look beautiful ,

635
00:56:59,457 --> 00:57:02,876
but there are plenty of shots where we had to prop them up .

636
00:57:03,002 --> 00:57:06,964
It was all hard work .

637
00:57:20,061 --> 00:57:26,567
( Yoshimura ) The reeds were so high .

638
00:57:28,778 --> 00:57:31,613
( Shindo ) They are about twice the height of a person .

639
00:57:33,283 --> 00:57:35,826
These are reeds .

640
00:57:38,037 --> 00:57:42,708
There were two types of reed ,

641
00:57:42,834 --> 00:57:45,586
as well as the susuki grass .

642
00:57:49,799 --> 00:57:54,970
( Yoshimura ) Someone said that it 's scary to run through

643
00:57:55,805 --> 00:58:01,977
the susuki grass , but it wasn 't just grass .

644
00:58:02,979 --> 00:58:06,148
There were reeds , too .

645
00:58:23,416 --> 00:58:27,044
( Shindo ) We built a well in order to film ,

646
00:58:29,797 --> 00:58:35,385
but it was destroyed

647
00:58:35,512 --> 00:58:39,640
in the typhoon .

648
00:58:42,143 --> 00:58:46,813
All kinds of things like that happened .

649
00:58:55,823 --> 00:58:57,991
He 's imitating the barking of a dog .

650
00:59:03,039 --> 00:59:08,919
( Yoshimura ) It 's so many years since I saw the film .

651
00:59:09,879 --> 00:59:12,589
There were so many love scenes !

652
00:59:12,715 --> 00:59:16,176
( Sato ) It 's surprising . ( Yoshimura ) I was surprised how many !

653
00:59:18,304 --> 00:59:25,852
( Sato ) They were necessary to show Nobuko 's jealousy .

654
00:59:37,156 --> 00:59:40,951
( Yoshimura ) I was so young ,

655
00:59:41,077 --> 00:59:45,455
and Kei had had his moxibustion treatment

656
00:59:49,711 --> 00:59:54,965
we both had magnificent bodies then .

657
01:00:00,763 --> 01:00:02,347
( Shindo ) Are you still doing it ?

658
01:00:02,473 --> 01:00:05,183
( Sato ) Not anymore . But the clinic 's still there .

659
01:00:06,644 --> 01:00:12,316
I mentioned it on the TV ,

660
01:00:12,442 --> 01:00:16,528
and I still get letters ,

661
01:00:16,654 --> 01:00:20,324
asking me where it is .

662
01:00:21,659 --> 01:00:23,535
( Shindo ) Does it really work ?

663
01:00:23,661 --> 01:00:25,954
( Sato ) If you do it seriously .

664
01:00:30,585 --> 01:00:32,711
You can 't do it half-heartedly ,

665
01:00:35,715 --> 01:00:38,342
it will have the opposite effect .

666
01:00:38,468 --> 01:00:42,095
You have to follow the instructions exactly .

667
01:00:42,221 --> 01:00:43,930
It takes one year .

668
01:00:48,019 --> 01:00:51,897
It won 't work if you give up halfway .

669
01:00:52,023 --> 01:00:57,027
You must be determined to change your condition .

670
01:00:58,363 --> 01:01:04,743
I gained weight , and it felt as if ...

671
01:01:05,662 --> 01:01:09,581
( Shindo ) That 's true for everything .

672
01:01:11,459 --> 01:01:17,089
Not just improving your health .

673
01:01:18,216 --> 01:01:22,969
( Sato ) It felt as if my cells themselves had changed .

674
01:01:29,227 --> 01:01:32,479
( Shindo ) Your cells ? Was your brain the same ?

675
01:01:32,605 --> 01:01:36,566
( Sato ) No , that got worse !

676
01:01:37,860 --> 01:01:40,862
I ate five meals a day .

677
01:01:43,199 --> 01:01:44,616
Mostly rice .

678
01:01:45,076 --> 01:01:50,580
I don 't know why , but rice was easy to digest .

679
01:01:50,707 --> 01:01:56,712
It took four hours to digest completely ,

680
01:01:56,838 --> 01:02:00,590
and so I had to eat every 4 hours .

681
01:02:01,926 --> 01:02:05,846
( Yoshimura ) Even during shooting ? ( Sato ) Yes .

682
01:02:07,181 --> 01:02:10,475
( Yoshimura ) I didn 't notice . ( Shindo ) Not on Onibaba , right ?

683
01:02:10,601 --> 01:02:14,771
( Sato ) That was when we shot Ningen .

684
01:02:15,398 --> 01:02:17,607
If you don 't eat at the right time ,

685
01:02:18,651 --> 01:02:24,281
the treatment will have the opposite effect .

686
01:02:25,158 --> 01:02:31,455
Because of the effect on the intestine

687
01:02:32,165 --> 01:02:36,793
unless food is eaten properly ,

688
01:02:37,712 --> 01:02:44,134
you will get an upset stomach .

689
01:02:44,927 --> 01:02:47,888
It can cause an abnormal gas ,

690
01:02:48,347 --> 01:02:51,516
which can fill the stomach

691
01:02:52,351 --> 01:02:56,480
and cause diarrhoea .

692
01:02:58,858 --> 01:03:00,942
( Yoshimura ) So you ate ... ?

693
01:03:01,068 --> 01:03:05,530
( Sato ) So I had to eat every four hours .

694
01:03:05,656 --> 01:03:10,827
( Shindo ) It was good for us , Kei-san ,

695
01:03:10,953 --> 01:03:14,080
because you lost that civilised look .

696
01:03:21,297 --> 01:03:25,133
( Sato ) If I hadn 't put on weight , I wouldn 't have been hired !

697
01:03:25,259 --> 01:03:27,427
I have moxibustion to thank for that !

698
01:03:27,553 --> 01:03:30,680
( Shindo ) And slowing your brain down was just right for the part !

699
01:03:30,807 --> 01:03:33,558
( Sato ) I was always slow-witted !

700
01:03:35,561 --> 01:03:40,190
( Shindo ) So you became more savage .

701
01:03:41,526 --> 01:03:43,318
( Sato ) I couldn 't get much slower !

702
01:03:43,444 --> 01:03:45,987
( Shindo ) Fundamentally , you are the scientific type .

703
01:03:47,490 --> 01:03:51,701
You had the treatment just in time then .

704
01:03:52,286 --> 01:03:56,289
The swaying grass is very effective .

705
01:03:58,251 --> 01:03:59,709
( Sato ) It 's very effective .

706
01:04:01,921 --> 01:04:04,631
( Yoshimura ) I think I must have run away .

707
01:04:07,969 --> 01:04:11,513
I must have run all the way back to Tokyo .

708
01:04:14,267 --> 01:04:18,061
( Shindo ) We could see the night sky in the distance illuminated by Tokyo .

709
01:04:21,691 --> 01:04:24,025
There was lightning , too .

710
01:04:24,151 --> 01:04:27,153
We all watched it ,

711
01:04:27,280 --> 01:04:34,119
and it made us want to go home back to Tokyo .

712
01:04:34,245 --> 01:04:39,791
But we kept on going .

713
01:04:43,921 --> 01:04:47,883
Hayashi 's music is dynamic .

714
01:04:48,342 --> 01:04:51,845
The mask was made

715
01:04:51,971 --> 01:04:55,849
by a famous mask maker in Kyoto .

716
01:04:56,726 --> 01:04:59,895
We had two made ,

717
01:05:00,021 --> 01:05:06,109
because one needs to be broken later .

718
01:05:08,779 --> 01:05:13,700
The mask maker is dead now , too .

719
01:05:14,452 --> 01:05:19,581
He made us a magnificent mask .

720
01:05:30,801 --> 01:05:34,679
The story is based on The Mask of Flesh story .

721
01:05:37,350 --> 01:05:41,394
The monk , Rennyo , was the 8th Patriarch

722
01:05:42,980 --> 01:05:46,274
of Shin Buddhism .

723
01:05:46,776 --> 01:05:49,986
Until then , the teachings of the sect were not well known ,

724
01:05:50,112 --> 01:05:52,781
so Rennyo set about to change that .

725
01:05:52,907 --> 01:05:56,701
He was a great communicator

726
01:05:56,827 --> 01:06:00,789
and had enormous vitality ,

727
01:06:00,915 --> 01:06:03,249
and , since there was no printing at that time ,

728
01:06:03,376 --> 01:06:05,168
he wrote hundreds of pages

729
01:06:05,294 --> 01:06:08,421
of stories every day to distribute to the people .

730
01:06:08,547 --> 01:06:12,425
One of the stories he wrote was the simple tale , The Mask of Flesh .

731
01:06:13,135 --> 01:06:16,846
A daughter-in-law regularly attended the temple .

732
01:06:17,348 --> 01:06:20,350
Her mother-in-law didn 't like it and tried to stop her ,

733
01:06:20,476 --> 01:06:24,562
by donning a mask to frighten her away from the temple .

734
01:06:24,689 --> 01:06:32,278
The Buddha punished her by making it impossible to remove the mask .

735
01:06:32,405 --> 01:06:36,658
When the daughter-in-law heard what had happened ,

736
01:06:36,784 --> 01:06:44,040
she prayed to the Buddha and the grip of the mask was released .

737
01:06:44,166 --> 01:06:47,961
In those days , daughter-in-laws were often

738
01:06:48,087 --> 01:06:51,673
treated badly by their in-laws .

739
01:06:51,799 --> 01:06:55,176
But they were important to produce the next generation .

740
01:06:56,762 --> 01:07:02,600
Rennyo thought that he could recruit followers by targeting these women .

741
01:07:04,770 --> 01:07:07,480
He wrote the story to warn in-laws

742
01:07:08,190 --> 01:07:12,235
against maltreating their daughters-in-law .

743
01:07:13,738 --> 01:07:17,490
( Sato ) I heard that story when I was young .

744
01:07:19,201 --> 01:07:21,745
I 'm from Aizu in Fukushima .

745
01:07:24,373 --> 01:07:30,462
My parents were in the Nichiren sect , I think .

746
01:07:30,588 --> 01:07:34,090
( Shindo ) It 's a famous Buddhist story .

747
01:07:34,967 --> 01:07:38,011
( Sato ) I heard it from my grandmother .

748
01:07:38,137 --> 01:07:43,433
( Shindo ) The story was actually written

749
01:07:43,559 --> 01:07:48,563
in Yoshizaki in Fukui Prefecture .

750
01:07:48,689 --> 01:07:53,860
The Shin Buddhists were being persecuted by another sect ,

751
01:07:53,986 --> 01:07:55,779
and Rennyo escaped there .

752
01:07:55,905 --> 01:08:01,701
He would return to challenge his persecutors later ,

753
01:08:02,244 --> 01:08:04,996
but while there , he wrote powerful tales ,

754
01:08:05,122 --> 01:08:11,753
such as this one as a means of attracting followers .

755
01:08:12,213 --> 01:08:17,008
It 's easy to understand for farming folk . It 's a simple story .

756
01:08:17,134 --> 01:08:22,639
( Sato ) It was no longer a religious story .

757
01:08:23,307 --> 01:08:26,059
It became a folk tale .

758
01:08:28,145 --> 01:08:32,065
( Shindo ) It 's been handed down over many years ,

759
01:08:32,817 --> 01:08:35,777
because of its simplicity

760
01:08:36,862 --> 01:08:42,992
and its universal human theme of the difficult relationship

761
01:08:43,452 --> 01:08:46,830
between a bride and her mother-in-law .

762
01:08:46,956 --> 01:08:50,500
It resonates to this day .

763
01:08:54,797 --> 01:08:57,132
As for the mask being used

764
01:08:57,258 --> 01:09:01,219
to hide the ugly face of a general ,

765
01:09:05,975 --> 01:09:08,935
that was my idea .

766
01:09:09,061 --> 01:09:13,648
I interpreted the story in a contemporary way .

767
01:09:13,774 --> 01:09:17,527
But that was the original story .

768
01:09:18,362 --> 01:09:23,908
A mother goes to the temple in the evening ,

769
01:09:24,034 --> 01:09:28,163
she listens to the sermon

770
01:09:29,582 --> 01:09:33,126
and falls asleep ,

771
01:09:34,295 --> 01:09:37,630
because the sermon is boring .

772
01:09:42,469 --> 01:09:45,513
The priest knows that ,

773
01:09:45,639 --> 01:09:50,185
and there is a tacit agreement between them .

774
01:09:51,020 --> 01:09:53,521
The priest makes his sermon boring ,

775
01:09:54,106 --> 01:09:59,611
so that the woman can sleep .

776
01:09:59,737 --> 01:10:05,200
She 's tired from her day 's work ,

777
01:10:05,326 --> 01:10:09,579
and comes to the temple

778
01:10:10,539 --> 01:10:12,957
in the evening for a rest .

779
01:10:16,378 --> 01:10:21,257
She can 't leave the children at home ,

780
01:10:22,092 --> 01:10:25,637
so she brings them to the temple , too .

781
01:10:25,763 --> 01:10:28,806
At the temple ,

782
01:10:28,933 --> 01:10:34,604
they are given a sweet bun ,

783
01:10:34,730 --> 01:10:42,237
so the children want to go to the temple to get the bun .

784
01:10:44,198 --> 01:10:50,203
As this is happening , their mother sleeps .

785
01:10:51,747 --> 01:10:56,125
Rennyo 's stories are like this .

786
01:10:56,835 --> 01:11:02,048
He appeals to the people 's instincts .

787
01:11:02,633 --> 01:11:05,009
They are clever stories .

788
01:11:07,346 --> 01:11:13,059
These old folk tales remain ,

789
01:11:13,185 --> 01:11:15,436
because they 're so powerful .

790
01:11:16,689 --> 01:11:20,066
The stories that had no power have long gone .

791
01:11:23,070 --> 01:11:26,281
It was a lot of trouble to make this hole .

792
01:11:29,702 --> 01:11:31,661
The ADs made it .

793
01:11:33,038 --> 01:11:35,665
( Sato ) Yes , I saw them .

794
01:11:40,045 --> 01:11:46,134
( Shindo ) That 's why they weren 't around the set when we were shooting .

795
01:11:48,178 --> 01:11:52,265
But I let them know that they were still

796
01:11:52,391 --> 01:11:55,727
contributing creatively to the film .

797
01:11:57,771 --> 01:12:02,608
Ah , this was the problem cut .

798
01:12:02,735 --> 01:12:08,239
( Yoshimura ) I was shocked when I saw the rushes .

799
01:12:08,365 --> 01:12:10,533
I asked you to cut it .

800
01:12:11,160 --> 01:12:14,412
( Shindo ) It was you who decided to strip off .

801
01:12:14,538 --> 01:12:17,540
( Yoshimura ) No , I was wearing skin-coloured tights ,

802
01:12:17,666 --> 01:12:22,337
and you said they were visible .

803
01:12:22,463 --> 01:12:26,924
You were using a telephoto lens .

804
01:12:27,051 --> 01:12:29,969
I didn 't know anything about the technical side of things ,

805
01:12:30,095 --> 01:12:35,266
I assumed you wouldn 't see from such a distance ,

806
01:12:35,392 --> 01:12:38,394
so I did it in the nude .

807
01:12:38,520 --> 01:12:40,938
When I saw the rushes ,

808
01:12:41,065 --> 01:12:46,027
you could see everything ,

809
01:12:46,153 --> 01:12:49,280
and I asked you to cut it .

810
01:12:49,406 --> 01:12:53,659
I can 't remember how you responded .

811
01:12:54,536 --> 01:13:00,458
I said they wouldn 't be able to show that in the cinemas .

812
01:13:00,584 --> 01:13:03,544
Then I was suddenly nominated

813
01:13:03,670 --> 01:13:06,798
for a Blue Ribbon Award for best supporting actress ,

814
01:13:06,924 --> 01:13:09,884
and I couldn 't say anything more .

815
01:13:10,010 --> 01:13:12,553
( Shindo ) I did cut it a little .

816
01:13:13,555 --> 01:13:17,433
We started shooting

817
01:13:17,559 --> 01:13:21,104
in the morning ,

818
01:13:21,688 --> 01:13:26,150
but it was too muddy to run properly .

819
01:13:26,944 --> 01:13:32,031
We laid boards down to cover the mud

820
01:13:32,157 --> 01:13:34,033
for you to run on .

821
01:13:34,159 --> 01:13:38,454
People were working in mud up to their waists

822
01:13:38,580 --> 01:13:43,876
and chests to solve the problem .

823
01:13:45,337 --> 01:13:47,713
You were inspired by their selfless efforts .

824
01:13:47,840 --> 01:13:49,757
( Yoshimura ) Really ? ( Shindo ) So you stripped off .

825
01:13:49,883 --> 01:13:54,345
( Yoshimura ) Really ? I don 't remember that .

826
01:13:54,471 --> 01:13:57,598
( Shindo ) Really . That was why !

827
01:13:59,309 --> 01:14:02,854
( Yoshimura ) I thought it was because of the tights ,

828
01:14:03,897 --> 01:14:09,652
and because the camera was so far away

829
01:14:09,778 --> 01:14:13,823
and you wouldn 't see .

830
01:14:13,949 --> 01:14:18,202
I thought it was the tights and the camera .

831
01:14:19,496 --> 01:14:23,875
( Sato ) No . I was right behind you .

832
01:14:24,001 --> 01:14:27,128
The camera was over to the left .

833
01:14:27,796 --> 01:14:33,801
You were responding to the way people had worked

834
01:14:34,303 --> 01:14:36,262
up to their chests in the mud .

835
01:14:36,388 --> 01:14:40,266
- You were impressed by that . - ( Yoshimura ) I 'd forgotten .

836
01:14:43,145 --> 01:14:46,647
( Sato ) I remember Shindo-san ,

837
01:14:47,232 --> 01:14:49,400
he was calling out to you

838
01:14:50,486 --> 01:14:55,114
and you stripped off boldly .

839
01:14:55,240 --> 01:14:59,660
We were all impressed .

840
01:15:04,833 --> 01:15:09,504
( Shindo ) It was hard getting that shot .

841
01:15:09,630 --> 01:15:13,716
I thought that shot was going to be easy ,

842
01:15:14,676 --> 01:15:17,678
but it wasn 't .

843
01:15:18,847 --> 01:15:24,727
We put three layers of board down .

844
01:15:24,853 --> 01:15:28,898
The actors waited all morning while we prepared it .

845
01:15:29,024 --> 01:15:32,193
There 's a sequel to this tale .

846
01:15:32,861 --> 01:15:36,906
When we screened the film for Toho ,

847
01:15:37,032 --> 01:15:42,119
Fujimoto cornered me and asked me

848
01:15:42,246 --> 01:15:47,291
what I was going to do about the censors .

849
01:15:47,417 --> 01:15:50,086
I said not to worry ,

850
01:15:50,712 --> 01:15:55,174
but I did end up

851
01:15:55,300 --> 01:15:58,010
cutting it a little bit .

852
01:16:00,764 --> 01:16:04,517
There was never any call for cuts ,

853
01:16:04,643 --> 01:16:09,647
and the few we made settled the matter anyway .

854
01:16:09,773 --> 01:16:15,152
We actually got on well and he helped out

855
01:16:15,946 --> 01:16:21,033
with the film 's distribution .

856
01:16:22,244 --> 01:16:25,746
Incidentally , I received the Fujimoto Award yesterday .

857
01:16:25,872 --> 01:16:28,040
( Yoshimura ) Congratulations !

858
01:16:28,166 --> 01:16:35,256
( Shindo ) I mentioned it because we talked about this story ,

859
01:16:40,095 --> 01:16:45,266
the story of the pubic hair ...

860
01:16:47,185 --> 01:16:51,063
( Yoshimura ) Two friends of mine

861
01:16:52,774 --> 01:16:56,652
saw the film at the theatre and told me

862
01:16:56,778 --> 01:17:01,198
that the scene didn 't look at all obscene .

863
01:17:01,325 --> 01:17:04,035
I was so relieved .

864
01:17:07,664 --> 01:17:09,665
They thought it was good .

865
01:17:09,791 --> 01:17:13,419
( Sato ) Some people who saw the film in the theatre

866
01:17:14,171 --> 01:17:17,798
said they could see my private parts

867
01:17:18,800 --> 01:17:21,552
when I was running .

868
01:17:21,678 --> 01:17:23,554
They must have had good eyesight ,

869
01:17:23,680 --> 01:17:27,808
I was wearing flesh-coloured pants !

870
01:17:27,934 --> 01:17:33,689
It 's not so easy for a man running naked , is it ?

871
01:17:34,524 --> 01:17:36,609
They wouldn 't believe me though .

872
01:17:39,112 --> 01:17:43,824
When it works well , the audience believes it 's real .

873
01:17:45,452 --> 01:17:48,579
( Shindo ) That scene was essential

874
01:17:48,705 --> 01:17:53,834
for the overall atmosphere of the film .

875
01:17:54,378 --> 01:18:00,341
( Yoshimura ) When I saw it , it wasn 't obscene .

876
01:18:01,510 --> 01:18:03,177
It was invigorating .

877
01:18:04,429 --> 01:18:08,974
( Shindo ) That 's down to your refreshing personality ,

878
01:18:09,434 --> 01:18:14,730
your graciousness . Yes . That 's the right expression .

879
01:18:15,857 --> 01:18:18,567
( Sato ) It was about what had been done .

880
01:18:18,694 --> 01:18:24,281
( Shindo ) Yes . We 'd worked hard from the morning .

881
01:18:24,741 --> 01:18:29,787
We 'd been laying the boards ,

882
01:18:29,913 --> 01:18:32,623
and that 's why you did it .

883
01:18:32,749 --> 01:18:37,420
( Yoshimura ) I 'd forgotten .

884
01:18:37,546 --> 01:18:44,552
So it was that everyone had worked so hard ,

885
01:18:45,887 --> 01:18:51,183
and the fact that you could see the tights as well .

886
01:18:54,354 --> 01:18:58,774
( Sato ) He didn 't say anything about tights .

887
01:18:58,900 --> 01:19:02,069
He just called out , " Hey , Jitsuko ! "

888
01:19:02,571 --> 01:19:07,199
And you got the message and stripped off .

889
01:19:08,702 --> 01:19:11,912
I was only 30cm behind you and I remember it .

890
01:19:15,709 --> 01:19:20,087
( Yoshimura ) I thought that it was because ...

891
01:19:20,213 --> 01:19:23,758
you said the tights were visible .

892
01:19:25,635 --> 01:19:30,806
( Shindo ) Anyway , it was good that you were so brave .

893
01:19:30,932 --> 01:19:34,727
It doesn 't look at all lewd .

894
01:19:36,438 --> 01:19:40,941
( Yoshimura ) It 's good that I didn 't think too much about it .

895
01:19:41,401 --> 01:19:46,322
It was only my third film ,

896
01:19:47,657 --> 01:19:50,576
and I didn 't know anything .

897
01:19:50,702 --> 01:19:55,915
In the end , you made it into an invigorating scene .

898
01:19:58,418 --> 01:20:03,339
( Shindo ) You had youth and vitality .

899
01:20:03,465 --> 01:20:05,633
It worked well .

900
01:20:05,759 --> 01:20:10,638
( Yoshimura ) I would have been embarrassed if it was in the studio ,

901
01:20:10,764 --> 01:20:15,017
but there was no one around and the camera was far away .

902
01:20:15,143 --> 01:20:18,854
( Sato ) It was a telephoto lens . ( Yoshimura ) I didn 't know that .

903
01:20:19,523 --> 01:20:23,651
I didn 't know about the camera .

904
01:20:24,402 --> 01:20:27,822
( Shindo ) The telephoto was hard to move around .

905
01:20:32,494 --> 01:20:38,457
But in the end , it was very effective .

906
01:20:39,835 --> 01:20:41,836
Everyone did their bit .

907
01:20:41,962 --> 01:20:45,881
There 's a scene

908
01:20:46,007 --> 01:20:50,386
where Nobuko embraces the tree .

909
01:20:50,512 --> 01:20:55,266
When I took a train from Abiko on the Narita Line ,

910
01:20:56,768 --> 01:21:01,522
I saw this dead pine tree

911
01:21:02,190 --> 01:21:08,654
at the side of the track near one of the stations .

912
01:21:09,155 --> 01:21:12,658
I thought it made an impressive sight ,

913
01:21:13,326 --> 01:21:17,997
and I decided to bring it to the set .

914
01:21:20,375 --> 01:21:24,545
The townspeople were happy to let us take it ,

915
01:21:24,671 --> 01:21:27,882
as it was already dead .

916
01:21:28,008 --> 01:21:30,342
The ADs couldn 't handle it on their own ,

917
01:21:33,096 --> 01:21:38,142
so the lighting and sound crew helped them

918
01:21:38,268 --> 01:21:41,478
to chop it down

919
01:21:42,063 --> 01:21:48,068
and to load it onto a lorry and bring it to the set .

920
01:21:48,778 --> 01:21:51,530
No one complained

921
01:21:51,656 --> 01:21:55,868
about doing that sort of thing .

922
01:21:55,994 --> 01:22:00,748
Everyone mucked in

923
01:22:00,874 --> 01:22:03,959
and no one complained .

924
01:22:08,214 --> 01:22:12,384
Felling and transporting trees is a job for a professional .

925
01:22:15,305 --> 01:22:22,144
People would have been within their rights to refuse ,

926
01:22:22,687 --> 01:22:26,357
but no one did .

927
01:22:26,483 --> 01:22:31,320
There are good and bad sides to it ,

928
01:22:33,782 --> 01:22:39,370
but this kind of group mentality once existed in the Japanese film world .

929
01:22:39,955 --> 01:22:43,832
We had to wait for the sun

930
01:22:43,959 --> 01:22:47,586
to set up here .

931
01:22:49,631 --> 01:22:53,926
You can 't do that sort of thing

932
01:22:54,052 --> 01:22:58,722
unless you have the time .

933
01:23:22,497 --> 01:23:25,040
( Yoshimura ) Nobuko was young then , too .

934
01:23:25,166 --> 01:23:28,877
( Shindo ) She was full of life , too .

935
01:23:30,005 --> 01:23:36,802
It 's seven years now since she died .

936
01:23:41,182 --> 01:23:44,184
( Sato ) Yes , it was 1994 , wasn 't it ?

937
01:23:50,233 --> 01:23:55,988
I met her at the Tennozu Art Sphere theatre just before she died .

938
01:24:00,285 --> 01:24:04,747
They were doing an English play and the director had come over .

939
01:24:05,206 --> 01:24:09,460
Nobuko came to see it .

940
01:24:09,586 --> 01:24:13,130
Togo Haruko was also in the play .

941
01:24:23,224 --> 01:24:26,226
Afterwards I thought

942
01:24:26,352 --> 01:24:31,356
it was as if she had come to say goodbye ,

943
01:24:31,483 --> 01:24:34,234
because she died right after that .

944
01:24:37,989 --> 01:24:42,076
( Shindo ) She was relatively fit up until her death .

945
01:24:44,454 --> 01:24:47,289
She went to the theatre

946
01:24:47,832 --> 01:24:51,835
and to discussion meetings .

947
01:24:51,961 --> 01:24:56,006
( Sato ) It was after The Last Note , wasn 't it ?

948
01:24:56,132 --> 01:24:57,883
( Shindo ) Yes .

949
01:24:58,968 --> 01:25:04,807
( Yoshimura ) She was already sick then , wasn 't she ?

950
01:25:04,933 --> 01:25:06,850
( Shindo ) That 's right .

951
01:25:06,976 --> 01:25:13,107
She was told she had 18 months to live ,

952
01:25:13,233 --> 01:25:17,111
and she did what work she could during that time .

953
01:25:17,237 --> 01:25:22,449
In the end , she ran out of strength .

954
01:25:25,995 --> 01:25:30,791
She didn 't suffer for too long .

955
01:25:32,710 --> 01:25:38,715
The doctors are usually right about cancer .

956
01:25:42,178 --> 01:25:45,430
It was the same for Mizoguchi and Ozu .

957
01:25:45,557 --> 01:25:49,560
They died when the doctors said they would .

958
01:25:55,358 --> 01:25:59,653
You saw where the demon appeared there .

959
01:26:00,238 --> 01:26:04,283
The choreography for that scene was arranged by Kanze Hideo .

960
01:26:05,785 --> 01:26:11,165
It has the feel of a scene from a Noh play .

961
01:26:11,291 --> 01:26:15,502
I wasn 't confident about choreographing that scene ,

962
01:26:16,296 --> 01:26:18,172
so I asked Kanze to help .

963
01:26:21,551 --> 01:26:28,807
You can hear the intense percussion

964
01:26:28,933 --> 01:26:33,103
and the voice yelling .

965
01:26:33,229 --> 01:26:35,230
That 's Kanze 's voice .

966
01:26:35,356 --> 01:26:37,649
( Sato ) Hideo 's voice ? ( Shindo ) Yes .

967
01:26:37,775 --> 01:26:40,986
And what a voice !

968
01:26:43,531 --> 01:26:46,825
It 's astounding !

969
01:26:46,951 --> 01:26:49,786
( Sato ) It would make the window panes vibrate .

970
01:26:49,913 --> 01:26:53,040
( Shindo ) It 's as if a banshee had appeared .

971
01:26:56,002 --> 01:26:59,421
The cry is drawn out ,

972
01:26:59,547 --> 01:27:04,134
leaving a long trail behind it .

973
01:27:04,260 --> 01:27:06,678
( Sato ) It 's a terrifying sound .

974
01:27:10,183 --> 01:27:14,019
( Shindo ) The rapid beat of the drum ,

975
01:27:14,145 --> 01:27:18,023
and then the voice .

976
01:27:18,149 --> 01:27:20,192
Hayashi composed it like that .

977
01:27:53,434 --> 01:27:55,894
Shige did the make-up .

978
01:27:59,274 --> 01:28:02,317
He was famous .

979
01:28:07,031 --> 01:28:11,994
( Yoshimura ) I remember when he went back to Tokyo .

980
01:28:12,787 --> 01:28:17,082
His assistant did Nobuko 's eyebrows ,

981
01:28:19,377 --> 01:28:22,754
but she didn 't like it .

982
01:28:22,880 --> 01:28:28,218
She waited till he came back

983
01:28:29,220 --> 01:28:31,179
to make her up ,

984
01:28:31,306 --> 01:28:34,808
before she would do a scene .

985
01:28:40,898 --> 01:28:44,359
( Shindo ) That 's because he

986
01:28:44,485 --> 01:28:49,281
because he was a veteran .

987
01:28:49,407 --> 01:28:54,619
He made people up based on how they would look on screen ,

988
01:28:55,705 --> 01:28:57,539
not how they looked there and then .

989
01:28:57,665 --> 01:29:01,543
You need experience to do that .

990
01:29:02,253 --> 01:29:04,838
Mind you , he was a difficult person .

991
01:29:05,548 --> 01:29:08,925
He wouldn 't do anything if he didn 't feel like it .

992
01:29:12,388 --> 01:29:17,059
But we worked together well

993
01:29:17,185 --> 01:29:21,313
for a long time .

994
01:29:21,898 --> 01:29:26,943
He would stay on location and make the hair

995
01:29:27,403 --> 01:29:29,446
and the beards and everything .

996
01:29:31,240 --> 01:29:38,914
He would do things like adding that patch of white

997
01:29:40,208 --> 01:29:43,960
to Nobuko 's hair .

998
01:29:44,587 --> 01:29:46,880
( Sato ) It 's fashionable these days .

999
01:29:48,716 --> 01:29:51,134
( Shindo ) It wouldn 't have been any good

1000
01:29:51,260 --> 01:29:54,429
if the hair had been completely white .

1001
01:30:02,313 --> 01:30:04,523
( Yoshimura ) This is before the typhoon , isn 't it ?

1002
01:30:04,649 --> 01:30:09,945
( Shindo ) Yes , we were able to shoot the wind as soon as it arrived ,

1003
01:30:10,071 --> 01:30:11,571
because we were there .

1004
01:30:12,448 --> 01:30:14,449
It was the same with the birds .

1005
01:30:14,575 --> 01:30:16,493
( Yoshimura ) They were ducks and herons , weren 't they ?

1006
01:30:16,619 --> 01:30:24,042
( Shindo ) If you 're not living there , you can 't film this kind of thing .

1007
01:30:25,670 --> 01:30:30,340
If you have to travel to the location to catch the typhoon ,

1008
01:30:30,466 --> 01:30:33,218
you 'll miss it .

1009
01:30:39,767 --> 01:30:46,731
If you 're there , you just film it when it happens .

1010
01:30:48,609 --> 01:30:54,531
When the wind blew from the south ,

1011
01:30:55,199 --> 01:31:02,789
the water level on the north side of the marsh rose by one metre .

1012
01:31:03,791 --> 01:31:07,252
That 's because the sea was to the south .

1013
01:31:09,964 --> 01:31:14,092
When that happened ,

1014
01:31:14,760 --> 01:31:22,893
the prefab we were staying in would often flood .

1015
01:31:23,853 --> 01:31:27,939
There were lots of crayfish there and they would come

1016
01:31:28,065 --> 01:31:30,442
into the house when the waters rose .

1017
01:31:30,568 --> 01:31:34,571
( Yoshimura ) I remember we dug a hole at night

1018
01:31:34,697 --> 01:31:40,452
and we would find crayfish in there in the morning .

1019
01:31:42,371 --> 01:31:48,710
We 'd take them out and fry them .

1020
01:31:50,796 --> 01:31:56,593
( Shindo ) You have to get the mud out of them first .

1021
01:31:56,719 --> 01:31:58,929
( Yoshimura ) We caught lots .

1022
01:31:59,055 --> 01:32:03,141
( Shindo ) They used to eat crayfish tempura after the war .

1023
01:32:10,024 --> 01:32:13,485
( Sato ) There was an elderly couple

1024
01:32:13,611 --> 01:32:19,783
who used to go out in a boat on the water .

1025
01:32:19,909 --> 01:32:22,327
They would come back

1026
01:32:22,453 --> 01:32:27,582
with a bucket full of crayfish .

1027
01:32:28,209 --> 01:32:32,462
I assumed that they sold them to the local noodle shop .

1028
01:32:33,339 --> 01:32:36,716
( Shindo ) They use them to make soup .

1029
01:32:41,055 --> 01:32:46,851
When you 've rinsed the mud off , they 're beautiful .

1030
01:32:51,399 --> 01:32:56,194
About the time we finished filming ,

1031
01:32:56,320 --> 01:33:01,199
lots of tiny little crayfish hatched out .

1032
01:33:06,706 --> 01:33:08,248
This was hard work .

1033
01:33:08,374 --> 01:33:12,877
( Sato ) We couldn 't shoot this in the swamp ,

1034
01:33:15,798 --> 01:33:18,883
so the ADs had to plant all these reeds .

1035
01:33:19,010 --> 01:33:22,345
That was quite a job !

1036
01:33:26,767 --> 01:33:29,311
( Shindo ) They were driven to despair at the end .

1037
01:33:31,647 --> 01:33:37,193
The wind wouldn 't blow so we used a large fan .

1038
01:33:38,195 --> 01:33:43,908
We had to make the wind and create the lightning .

1039
01:33:46,120 --> 01:33:49,205
That was tough work .

1040
01:33:54,795 --> 01:33:58,923
And it was pouring with rain .

1041
01:34:07,099 --> 01:34:12,020
The field was extremely deep ,

1042
01:34:12,146 --> 01:34:16,775
and there were plenty of reeds .

1043
01:34:38,839 --> 01:34:43,718
What was this fellow 's name ? I can 't remember it ...

1044
01:35:10,621 --> 01:35:13,623
( Yoshimura ) That was the end of Hachi .

1045
01:35:36,856 --> 01:35:39,023
( Shindo ) They still used this method to make fire

1046
01:35:39,150 --> 01:35:41,609
in the countryside when I was a boy .

1047
01:35:44,071 --> 01:35:47,115
When they got cold in the fields ,

1048
01:35:47,241 --> 01:35:52,829
they would collect pine needles

1049
01:35:52,955 --> 01:35:56,332
and use a flint to light the fire .

1050
01:36:15,144 --> 01:36:17,771
- Do you smoke , Kei-san ? - ( Sato ) Yes .

1051
01:36:20,649 --> 01:36:24,486
( Shindo ) How much ? ( Sato ) A day ?

1052
01:36:24,612 --> 01:36:28,072
I 'd say about thirty a day .

1053
01:36:33,204 --> 01:36:35,955
Although I cough at the same time !

1054
01:36:38,793 --> 01:36:43,338
( Shindo ) Do you need to smoke now ? ( Sato ) No , I 'm fine .

1055
01:37:07,488 --> 01:37:13,618
( Shindo ) We had two of these masks made .

1056
01:37:13,744 --> 01:37:18,039
I went to Kyoto to order them myself .

1057
01:37:18,165 --> 01:37:21,459
I explained the situation

1058
01:37:21,585 --> 01:37:25,755
and had them made

1059
01:37:26,340 --> 01:37:30,760
at a good price ,

1060
01:37:32,263 --> 01:37:39,060
because of the film 's low budget .

1061
01:37:39,186 --> 01:37:44,274
( Yoshimura ) It 's an excellent mask . It has such an expression .

1062
01:37:44,775 --> 01:37:50,697
It has real expression when Nobuko wears it .

1063
01:37:51,699 --> 01:37:54,659
( Shindo ) Kanze Hideo praised it as well .

1064
01:37:54,785 --> 01:38:00,123
He tried it on one time

1065
01:38:00,249 --> 01:38:02,625
and performed for us .

1066
01:38:07,631 --> 01:38:10,717
( Sato ) Do you still have it ? ( Shindo ) Yes , I have it at home .

1067
01:38:12,303 --> 01:38:18,182
( Yoshimura ) The perfect one ? ( Shindo ) And the broken one , too .

1068
01:38:19,518 --> 01:38:25,356
I took it back and had it joined together again .

1069
01:38:25,482 --> 01:38:29,652
The maker was very attached to it , so he fixed it for me .

1070
01:38:47,671 --> 01:38:50,423
( Sato ) This was all post-recorded , wasn 't it ?

1071
01:38:50,549 --> 01:38:53,092
( Shindo ) That 's right . ( Sato ) The love scenes , too .

1072
01:38:53,218 --> 01:38:55,261
And the kisses .

1073
01:38:56,847 --> 01:39:00,516
My arms were black and blue

1074
01:39:02,269 --> 01:39:04,520
by the time I 'd finished recording .

1075
01:39:06,690 --> 01:39:09,233
( Shindo ) You have to get the timing just right .

1076
01:39:15,240 --> 01:39:19,494
( Sato ) You said that dubbing the sound would be easier ,

1077
01:39:19,620 --> 01:39:24,749
as we could repeat if required .

1078
01:39:27,711 --> 01:39:30,505
That 's not what the actors thought .

1079
01:39:31,548 --> 01:39:36,135
( Shindo ) Well , I had to persuade you somehow !

1080
01:39:42,810 --> 01:39:46,896
I had to get you to do it .

1081
01:40:03,038 --> 01:40:06,457
It 's impossible to synchronise things ,

1082
01:40:06,583 --> 01:40:10,336
with the grass swaying and the ground below all muddy .

1083
01:40:10,462 --> 01:40:12,046
( Sato ) Yes , that 's impossible .

1084
01:40:26,812 --> 01:40:31,315
- It was the same with Ningen . - ( Shindo ) Ningen , too , with the sea !

1085
01:40:31,442 --> 01:40:33,901
Impossible to synchronise .

1086
01:40:42,995 --> 01:40:45,955
( Yoshimura ) You remember so much , Kei-san .

1087
01:40:46,081 --> 01:40:49,208
You never fail to impress me .

1088
01:41:07,227 --> 01:41:11,522
( Shindo ) The make-up is good here ,

1089
01:41:14,443 --> 01:41:16,569
when the mask is stripped off .

1090
01:41:21,658 --> 01:41:24,827
The skin looks worn .

1091
01:41:46,934 --> 01:41:52,563
( Yoshimura ) Ah , is that Kanze 's voice ? ( Shindo ) That 's right . That 's his yell .

1092
01:42:01,448 --> 01:42:06,661
The point here is that , when the film ends ,

1093
01:42:06,787 --> 01:42:13,626
we know that Jitsuko leapt across , but we don 't know if Nobuko made it .

1094
01:42:14,711 --> 01:42:17,547
Nobody knows .

1095
01:42:24,096 --> 01:42:28,724
( Yoshimura ) So I was the only one left ? ( Shindo ) That 's right .

